:: Lab 1 (unavailable students)

(metadata:
"title", "Catching a Junior Apprentice",
"cardDesc", "Will they be able to help you?",
"img", "",
)

$cssColumnParent[

$cssColumnChild[
	$cssBox[
    	($funcImage: (passage: "S: Lab 1 (unavailable)")'s img)
         $cssBoxItem[''(print: (passage:)'s title )''<br>(print: (passage:)'s cardDesc)]
    ]
]

$cssColumnChild[

<!--randomize speaker based on $stuff's lighthouseDice (so that it only randomizes when clicking through a passage but not upon dipping in and out of menus)-->
(set: _speaker to (cond:
$stuff's lighthouseDice is 1, 1,
$stuff's lighthouseDice is 2, 2,
$stuff's lighthouseDice is 3, 3, 1
))
<!--enchant speaker lines-->
($funcNPCSpeakManual: "genericStudent" + (str:_speaker))
<!--hook name-->
(set: _line to (hook: "genericStudent" + (str:_speaker) + "Line"))


<!--content begins-->

<!--tracker A line-->
(cond:
$stuff's lighthouseTrackerA is 3, [{
You hail a group of students, and they immediately disperse, leaving the slowest or perhaps the boldest among them to face you down.
}],
$stuff's lighthouseTrackerA is 2, [{
Trying again, you catch up with another student. This one is carrying a heavy stack of books, who startled at your approach, almost dropping the books and crushing your feet.
}],
$stuff's lighthouseTrackerA is 1, [{
Like an snakecat in ambush, you wait in a corner of the hallway, until you hear the footsteps. You appear, quicker than they can run. Well, quicker than at least one of them.
}],
)
<br>

<!--student reply-->
(cond:
_speaker is 1, [{
_line["(either: "Du-don't know. N-new to Apesai. A-ask big s-sister.", "Library? Lab? Bed? You are teacher, but you don't know? Then how would student know?", "Where is lab? Why? Ask big sister to get in.", "Is this school? Yes, it is school. There are classes, student must go.", "Ask the Nurandah people. Ask others. I will not help.", "Ah, yes, //facilities// - that's the word. Hm... facilities are all around. Ask big sister if you want.", "No problem, you go up, and then... erm... You can find it yourself, not hard. But attendants - watch out. Sorry.")"]
<br>
(either: "The student before you is a small child with terracotta skin - a native, one of many, and a little bit too young for school. One must wonder if the davehmars here are having a hard time finding readier students.", "His Nurango sentences are curt, utilitarian. You wonder if it is a pattern from his Askavan tongue, or if the native students actually speak in poetry when alone with one another.", "The apprentice keeps fixing her cap and gown, trying to get all of her thick, silver hair underneath the wraps, clearly unfamiliar with Nurandah clothing.", "You've never met a native Askavan before, but now that you're in the very capital of the dahak, they seem to be unavoidable. This student is just one of many.", "An Askavan, one of many. You wonder if this school was originally meant to board native students, and the others - imperials - were merely an afterthought.", "This apprentice could barely speak Nurango. You wonder how lessons would proceed, and how much the students could absorb if every other student was like this one.")
}],
_speaker is 2, [{
_line["(either: "Erm, the lab? I don't know if I should... Who //are// you? I'm not sure strangers should be wandering around. You should talk to one of the teachers.", "Is this a school? Yes, it is. Why are you asking? Uh, listen, I better get to class. I'm already as late as it is.", "I just enrolled last month. I want to help, but truth is, I still ask the assistant where the washroom is, so...", "You should try the assistant. She does everything around here. I'd like to help, but I've got some chores right now. Sorry.", "You want to use the school facilities? Why, aren't you studying here? You're not? Oh. Then you should talk to someone else about that. I don't control the attendants, sorry.")"]
<br>
(either: "The apprentice is wearing a blue-and-white sash - the colors of the Reclaimers. Her parents are probably living in a frontier settlement in the deserts to the north. She has it far better than them.", "This student is wearing a gold knife on one of his ears. Is he a Yavanid? Or is he merely copying the neighborhood minstrel? Hard to tell where tradition ends and fashion begins in a place as mixed as Apesai.", "With both black hair of Nurandah and copper skin of Askava, it is difficult to place this student's ethnicity. But perhaps the classic descriptions you've learned from textbooks have not accounted for centuries of co-existence.", "This one is an imperial - you can be sure from her dark hair and pale features. However, you are less sure if she has only recently arrived since the Reclamation, or if her family has had roots here since the Second, or even First Colony Era.", "He is sufficiently well-spoken, albeit with an accent. Must be from an old family here in Askava, going back to the Second, or even First Colony Era.")
}],
_speaker is 3, [{
_line["(either: "Hmm? Why are you speaking to me? Shouldn't the adminstrators be handling new teachers? Excuse me.", "Oh, the school is a tower. There's only up and down. I'm sure if you keep climbing, you'll get to where you need to be. Now, if you'll excuse me, I also have somewhere I need to be.", "Tsk, I am a magus, not a tour guide. Of course I can call myself a 'magus'; I've already completed my basics. Now, if you'll excuse me...", "The school facilities... hm... I'm sure the assistant can help you. Yes, the //principal's// assistant. She's always around somewhere, if not the market.", "How did you get through the attendants? Oh that's right, there aren't any at the front gate. They should really fix that. Tch, why did my parents make me go here? Lousy...", "I'm sorry, but who //are// you? A journeyman? //Here//? In Apesai? That's great for you, really, but you should speak to one of the administrators. Or maybe their lap- I mean, assistant.")"]
<br>
(either: "You didn't expect to hear the Sanurango accent in this place, which this student is definitely trying to exaggerate. Aristocrats are the same anywhere - they cannot help themselves.", "The apprentice's gown is so fine that you wonder if it is breaking some kind of dress code. But then again, rules often bend around those whose parents can afford them such nice clothes.", "Black hair and fair skin: this apprentice is unmistakably Nurandahid. After being surrounded by foreigners, the sight of an imperial comes as a shock to you.", "You have met many of these types back in university - refined, cosmopolitan, and above it all. Still, despite their storied lineage, an aristocrat who has to study in Apesai cannot be all that important. Otherwise, they would have had better picks elsewhere.",)
}],
)
<br>

<!--another tracker A line-->
(cond:
$stuff's lighthouseTrackerA is 3, [{
You let the apprentice go. You, too, were clueless when you were at this age, which was not too long ago.
}],
$stuff's lighthouseTrackerA is 2, [{
Unable to get anything more out of this apprentice, you turn and leave. You tell yourself that it is not their job to welcome you, but then again, you would expect //some// respect for their senior. 
}],
$stuff's lighthouseTrackerA is 1, [{
You let the student go before you get any more frustrated. Doesn't anyone know anything? Do these provincial types have no sense of hospitality?
}],
)
<br>

<!--content ends-->



---
<!--run code for dynamic choices, using $stuff as tracker-->
(display: "code.lighthouseUnavailableChoices")

]<!--end child-->
]<!--end parent-->